(a) whether Government is aware that there is a shortage of trauma care facilities in public health institutions in many districts of the Vidarbha region of Maharashtra, particularly in the Nagpur Division;
(b) the existing number of vacant posts of specialist doctors, Civil Surgeons and paramedical staff in the Vidarbha region and the steps being taken to fill these vacancies in a time-bound manner; and
(c) whether Government proposes to implement any comprehensive plan for the expansion and strengthening of trauma centres in the Vidarbha region?

(a) whether Government is aware that, due to the shortage of Allopathic doctors in many Primary Health Centres in the Vidarbha region, AYUSH doctors are providing healthcare services through the fusion of AYUSH and Allopathic services;
(b) the steps being taken by Government in Nagpur and the Vidarbha region to ensure the availability of the necessary training, medicines, equipment and other resources to AYUSH doctors discharging additional responsibilities; and
(c) whether Government proposes to formulate any policy to define the role of AYUSH doctors in National Health Programmes and public health activities?

(a) whether Government is aware that the utilization of Government houses available under the Affordable Rental Housing Complexes (ARHC) scheme has been significantly lower than expected;
(b) whether special steps are being taken to promote ARHC projects in the industrial and educational zones of Nagpur and Vidarbha;
(c) whether Government proposes to prioritize proximity of industrial areas and higher educational institutions for ARHC projects; and
(d) the current status of the implementation of technology innovation grants and the Model Tenancy Act under ARHC?

(a) whether Government proposes to conduct a comprehensive safety and structural review of the old and major dams in the Vidarbha region;
(b) if so, the proposed timeline and the details of the concerned agencies;
(c) whether risks related to ageing infrastructure, siltation or maintenance have been identified in previous studies; and
(d) the steps being taken to ensure long-term dam safety in view of climate change and rainfall uncertainty?
